// Project: occupant behavior in BIM-to-BEM workflows. Type: schema mapping, read left to right.
// Idea, Building Simulation 2025, 3.2: "a gbXML-to-obXML schema translator that reuses BIM models from gbXML files to
// generate obXML documents for implementing OB simulation."
// Labels and sources (Building Simulation 2025, md copy):
//   gb-obXML converter; validate, map, validate   4.2: validates the gbXML input, "transforms ... according to
//                                                  predefined mapping rules", "validates the generated obXML document"
//   gbXML v7.04, obXML v1.4                        4.2 ("gbXML v7.04 schema"); abstract ("obXML schema v1.4")
//   Building to Building                           5.3.2: "mapped the Campus/Building element in gbXML to the
//                                                  Buildings/Building element in obXML"
//   Space to Space                                 5.3.2: "Space identification was preserved"
//   Systems under Space; Zone to Systems           5.3.2: "creating a dedicated Systems element under each Space. HVAC-
//                                                  related information was transformed from the zone level in the
//                                                  gbXML to space-level system representations in obXML"
//   Zone to Zone, new in v1.4                      4.1.1: "the Zone element is newly introduced"; 5.3.2: "thermal design
//                                                  parameters in zones were accurately maintained"
//   Schedule to Schedule, new in v1.4              4.1.1: "the hierarchical structure of the schedules was directly
//                                                  adopted in the obXML schema"; 5.3.2: "preserved schedule references"
// Element names are the paper's; Building stands for Campus/Building and Buildings/Building.
// Fine-line diagram (classes .dgf in global.css), shared 300 x 356 frame with the other project diagrams.
